{
  "id": "06-listen-and-write",
  "title": "Listen, Write, and Act",
  "tenet": "Offer your goals to God",
  "durationMs": 46560,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/06-listen-and-write.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/06-listen-and-write.json",
  "text": "A woman brought a notebook to prayer because she did not want a good thought to disappear. She first asked for mercy and guidance. Then she sat in quiet attention. She wrote down what came to mind, without treating every thought as a command from God. Later, she weighed those notes against Scripture, love, wisdom, and the counsel of trusted people. You can practice this with an important goal. Name it clearly. Set a daily or weekly time. Begin by committing the period to God. Keep a notebook ready. Listen, write, and discern. End by choosing one faithful step. If nothing comes, the time is not wasted. Remaining with God can train the heart to hear, to love, and to serve.",
